# AI/LLM files
CONTEXT.md
AGENTS.md
.roo/
.idex/

# Miscellaneous files
.etc/

# Backups
*.bak

# Live configs (allow examples)
# This glob supersedes the previous per-file list (teams.yaml,
# compute-runtime-policies.yaml) and covers any future config too.
terraform/config/*.yaml
!terraform/config/*.example.yaml

# Local diagnostic scripts (never committed)
scripts-local/

# Local test scratch (never committed).
#
# `.testtmp/` holds throwaway harness scripts and JSON fixtures derived from
# live tenant responses. Fixtures can contain live resource and account names,
# so they must not be committed. It lives inside the repo rather than /tmp so
# that everything a task touches stays within the workspace.
.testtmp/

# Test-data seeder for workflow 9 (never committed).
#
# `.testdata/` creates and deletes REAL objects in the Prisma Cloud tenant.
# That tenant is SHARED - 145 container rules owned by 18 different engineers,
# several named after real customers - so the seeder is namespaced `tf9-test-`
# and refuses to touch anything else. It is gitignored because it holds live
# console URLs and captured API responses, and because a copy of it running
# with someone else's prefix is exactly the accident to avoid.
.testdata/

# Cached vendor documentation (never committed).
#
# `docs/` holds Markdown pulled from docs.prismacloud.io for offline reference
# while designing against the product's behaviour. It is third-party content, it
# goes stale, and it would otherwise dwarf the repo's own docs in any diff.
# The distilled, durable findings live in plans/ and are committed; this is the
# raw source material behind them.
docs/

# Workflow run artifacts. These are produced inside terraform/ by the read-only
# workflows and must never be committed - alert-summary.json in particular
# contains live resource names. The nested terraform/.gitignore that used to
# cover the plan files was removed in the repo cleanup, so they are listed here.
terraform/tfplan
terraform/plan-output.txt
terraform/handled-failure.marker
terraform/alert-summary.json
terraform/access-audit.json
terraform/tenant-inventory.json

# The digest artifact. This one is not merely "live resource names": when the
# grace warning is planned it embeds `would_notify`, the cloudAccountOwners
# read off the alerts - real, live mailboxes of real people, including
# addresses outside the company. It must never be committed.
terraform/runtime-grace-digest.json
terraform/compute-alert-summary.json
terraform/runtime-rule-effects.json

# Terraform plan files in JSON form, ANYWHERE in the tree - not just under
# terraform/. `terraform show -json tfplan` embeds the `variables` block
# verbatim, so a plan JSON contains the Prisma Cloud access key, secret key
# and console URL in PLAINTEXT on its first line. The entries above are all
# `terraform/`-prefixed and a plan saved at the repo root slipped past every
# one of them. These patterns are deliberately unanchored.
plan.json
*.tfplan
*.tfplan.json

# macOS
.DS_Store

# Editor / IDE
.idea/
.vscode/
*.swp
*~

# Python virtualenvs
.venv/
__pycache__/
*.pyc

# Secrets / local config
.env
.env.*
*.pem
*.key

# Terraform working directory / state
**/.terraform/
**/.terraform.tfstate.lock.info
**/*.tfstate
**/*.tfstate.*
**/*.tfvars
**/*.tfvars.json
!**/*.tfvars.example
crash.log
crash.*.log
